            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "Looks like the `autocmd` was working, but the highlights were persisted:\r\n\r\n```txt\r\nNote: after disabling there might be highlighting left; it will be removed after next highlighting update (see |events| and `MiniTrailspace` |augroup|).\r\n```\r\n\r\nThis seems to be working, but I'm open to better solutions:\r\n\r\n```lua\r\n{\r\n  \"echasnovski/mini.trailspace\",\r\n  event = \"BufRead\",\r\n  opts = {},\r\n  init = function()\r\n    -- Hide trailing spaces in Lazy plugin buffer\r\n    -- Tip: check FileType with `:set filetype?`\r\n    vim.cmd \"autocmd FileType lazy lua require('mini.trailspace').unhighlight()\"\r\n  end,\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\nFrom my dotfiles: https://github.com/KyleKing/nvim/commit/dbafb26cf22ea6648059adb18aa3b1c1d61fad80",
