        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> This seems to be working, but I'm open to better solutions:\r\n\r\nYes, this is a suggested solution. Setting buffer local variable will make sure that highlighting will not be added in the future. As 'mini.trailspace' can not track setting a buffer local variable in a reasonable way, it can not know when to automatically undo possibly present highlighting. Thus calling `unhighlight()` once is the solution here.\r\n\r\nI would still suggest doing both buffer-local variable and unhighlighting:\r\n```lua\r\nvim.cmd('autocmd FileType lazy lua vim.b.minitrailspace_disable = true; MiniTrailspace.unhighlight()')\r\n```",
